      "message": "fix(mcp): the ui link verifies the peer by transport, not by a disclosed token\n\nThe review of PR #3971 (#3874) showed the token-proof hello cannot\nwork: the client sends the token to the peer before the peer proves\nanything, so a false server that never read the discovery file still\nreceives the token and computes the proof. No exchange over an open\nport fixes that, because the first client gives the secret away.\n\n- Windows: the link listens on a named pipe with a user-only ACL\n  (link_pipe, link_pipe_acl, link_pipe_stream); the CLI asks the\n  kernel which process serves the pipe and refuses a peer that is\n  not the process the file names, before one byte of the token\n  crosses. A \"tcp\" entry is refused by name on every platform. The\n  nonce/proof exchange is removed.\n- One elapsed deadline covers the whole hello exchange\n  (link_peer::read_line_bounded); a peer that trickles bytes ends\n  within it.\n- A line that reaches the 1 MiB bound without its newline closes the\n  link; no remainder is read as a new message.\n- The bridge's byte bound is a visible failure when the session was\n  still open, never a quiet success after a truncated answer.\n\nThe decision record is docs/decisions/3874-ui-link-transport.md.\n\nFixes #3874",
      "tree": {
